note (Zeki #5396 nonblocking qualification; not a gate): the warm-up early stop applies to guarded clients only (src/players/decision.rs:479 at 959a8a2: `self.guard.is_some() && guard::is_stop`). Without --guard the warm-up is as in 0e66836: a refused reservation (budget::BudgetCap, now a typed error with an unchanged message) is retried every 10 s up to 900 s; so the round-2 qualification that the typed BudgetCap stops an unguarded warm-up at once does not hold at source. The no-guard differences that do exist (959a8a2, for a player with its own budget, i.e. the Drex/Nace ledger): an error reply or a 200 with incomplete usage whose body reports usage.cost is booked at max(worst case, that charge) instead of the worst case; an error status documented as unbilled whose body reports a charge is booked at it instead of nothing. Also recorded in tools/v3/repeats/METADATA.
